{{/* @dot github.com/donseba/go-partial/examples/docs.DocsPage */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400 text-[13px] font-extrabold uppercase text-emerald-300">Integration</p>
    <h1 class="max-w-4xl text-5xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-slate-50">Server-sent events</h1>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400 max-w-4xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">SSE is a streaming writer layer. It does not replace connectors; it sends events after your handler decides what changed.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Patch a rendered partial</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">Use <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">sse.NewWriter</code> to apply the expected event-stream headers, then render a partial into a <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:patch</code> event.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">events := sse.NewWriter(w)

notice := partial.NewID("notice", "templates/notice.gohtml").
    SetDot(Notice{Message: "Saved"})

_ = events.PatchPartial(r.Context(), r, "#notice", notice)
_ = events.Signal("saved", true)
events.Flush()</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">PatchPartial</code> renders the partial itself, whatever the request targets. A partial that is not in a tree renders with the functions, stages and models of the application's root through <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">events.SetParent(root)</code>, which changes neither the partial nor the root.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Client listener</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The default event names are neutral. Your client can decide whether to replace <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">outerHTML</code>, update state, or hand the HTML to another library.</p>

    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">const stream = new EventSource("/events")

stream.addEventListener("partial:patch", (event) =&gt; {
    const patch = JSON.parse(event.data)
    document.querySelector(patch.target).outerHTML = patch.html
})

stream.addEventListener("partial:signal", (event) =&gt; {
    console.log(JSON.parse(event.data))
})</code></pre>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Event names and headers</h2>
    <table class="w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-800/90 text-left">
        <thead class="bg-slate-900"><tr><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Constant</th><th class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 text-left font-bold text-slate-50">Meaning</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">HeaderContentType</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">Content-Type</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">ContentTypeEventStream</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">text/event-stream</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">EventPatch</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:patch</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">EventSignal</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:signal</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">EventError</code></td><td class="border-b border-slate-700 px-3 py-2.5 align-middle"><code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:error</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Why it is not a connector</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">A connector interprets one request and writes one response. SSE keeps the response open and writes many events, so it is better as an explicit writer that can still render normal partials.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Concurrency notes</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">An <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">sse.Writer</code> owns one HTTP response stream. If several goroutines produce updates, serialize calls through your own channel or mutex so event frames are not interleaved. Partial rendering can still use the request context for cancellation and request-scoped sinks before each event is written.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Browser client</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">The browser client, served from <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clients.FS()</code>, is a small script that applies <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:patch</code> events with every connector, dispatches <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:signal</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:error</code> as DOM events, and opens a stream for elements with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-partial-stream</code> while they are in the page. Patched content is processed by htmx when it is loaded.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">mux.Handle("GET /assets/", http.StripPrefix("/assets/", http.FileServerFS(clients.FS())))

&lt;script src="/assets/partial-sse.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;ul id="activity" data-partial-stream="/activity/events"&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">A patch replaces its target (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">outerHTML</code>).</p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Hidden tabs and changing URLs</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">A stream follows its element: when the URL in <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-partial-stream</code> changes, the client streams from the new one. With <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-partial-stream-hidden="30s"</code>, the stream closes once the tab has been hidden that long (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:stream:paused</code>) and opens again when it shows, with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:stream:reconnect</code> on the element, so the page can fetch what it missed.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;aside id="presence" data-partial-stream="/events/presence" data-partial-stream-hidden="30s"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;</code></pre>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-50">Client ids and the back/forward cache</h2>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">With <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-partial-stream-client-id="tab"</code>, the client adds an id of the browser tab to the stream URL as that parameter, the same for the life of the page, so the server tells the tabs of one browser apart; scripts read it as <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">goPartialSSE.clientId</code>. A page restored from the back/forward cache opens its streams again, with <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">partial:stream:reconnect</code>.</p>
    <pre class="overflow-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 p-4 text-slate-100 shadow-2xl"><code class="block border-0 bg-transparent p-0 font-mono text-sm text-inherit">&lt;div data-partial-stream="/presence?page=/admin/pages" data-partial-stream-client-id="tab"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
    <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">With <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-partial-stream-beacon="/presence"</code> the client POSTs <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">clientId</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">params</code> (the stream URL's query) and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">reason</code> to that address: <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">beat</code> every <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">data-partial-stream-beat="15s"</code>, also while the tab is hidden, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">hidden</code>, <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">removed</code> and <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">pagehide</code>; <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">sse.ReadBeacon(r)</code> reads one. <code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">{{ "{{ sseAttrs url \"clientId\" \"tab\" \"hidden\" \"30s\" }}" }}</code> (<code class="rounded border border-sky-400/20 bg-sky-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-sky-100">sse.FuncMap()</code>) writes the client's attributes.</p>
</article>
